> Can you post a YAAP about your 11500 turn "Fastest" ascension?

Marvin once ascended in (I think) 8000 turns.

> Did anything unusual happen?

It might have been faster if the tournament had allowed the "monsters" option 
to be settable, as normal.  I like to set ghosts and shades to 'X', so they 
easily show up on telepathy and I know when I've found a bones level.  Anyway, 
I bypassed a bonepile when digging down to the castle.  There was a suspicious 
monster arrangement, but I was too lazy to use the ; command on every blank 
space to see if it was possibly a ghost (that is Marvin's strategy).  

Eventually I did re-encounter the bonespile, and it provided enough generic 
loot to prepare me for the final run.  But I had wasted some post-castle time 
in other levels, which of course had much lower loot/turn ratios.

There were of course plenty of turns wasted by my mistakes.  With perfect play 
this could easily have been a 4 digit ascension (9999 turns or less).  The 
luck factor was certainly slightly higher than in my previous two ascensions, 
but I am also making different strategic decisions, like skipping the last 3 
levels of Sokoban and not exploring dark Mines levels.


While I was putting my kit together I felt something was missing but couldn't 
figure out what.  Eventually, after I ran out of ?oG, it dawned on me that I 
had forgotten to make SDSM.  So I figured I'd have to watch out for my items 
being blown up by lightning, fire, cold, but as long as I was careful to keep 
stuff bagged it should be low risk....   

A black dragon on lvl 49 disintegrated my robe, my shirt, and my "oLS.  The 
blast reflected, but luckily missed me.  So I gated back to the main dungeon 
and wandered around dipping out fountains and exploring the levels I'd dug 
through.  I didn't find what I needed.  I gated to Sokoban, landed next to a 
iron piercer, killed it, and it dropped an already-blessed magic lamp.


On the Planes I had no good ways to confuse myself.  I like to use cursed 
food, especially eggs and tripe rations, but I had run out.  So I used 
alchemy: 3!oJuice + !oSpeed = 3!oBooze.  And on water I cursed a scroll of 
confuse monster.

The first altar was the correct one.


